        <templateparamlist>
          <param>
            <type>class <ref refid="NEW__ControlDependenceGraph_8C_1af40713911bb5d86f82a7057cc45a65ff" kindref="member">T</ref></type>
          </param>
          <param>
            <type>class Visitor</type>
          </param>
        </templateparamlist>
        <type>auto</type>
        <definition>auto Sawyer::Tree::Vertex&lt; B &gt;::traversePre</definition>
        <argsstring>(const Visitor &amp;visitor)</argsstring>
        <name>traversePre</name>
        <param>
          <type>const Visitor &amp;</type>
          <declname>visitor</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Pre-order forward traversal.</para><para>Perform a depth-first pre-order traversal. The functor is called once for each vertex before any of its children are traversed. This is equivalent to the <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Tree_1_1Vertex_1ad7be4e76c4377d761b492d1992d204c1" kindref="member">traverse</ref> traversal where the functor checks that the event is an <computeroutput>ENTER</computeroutput> event before doing anything. If the functor returns a value which evaluates to true in Boolean context, then the traversal immediately returns that value, otherwise it continues until the entire subtree is visited and returns a default-constructed value. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
